#### 8. Exception Handling in Tests — `addNullSkuManualCatch`

Manual `try`/`catch`/`fail` reimplements what `assertThrows` provides out of the box. If the `catch` is too broad, it can mask unexpected exceptions.

```java
// Lines 93-98
try {
    catalog.add(null, 1);
    fail("should have thrown");
} catch (Exception ex) {
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

**Fix:** Use JUnit 5's `assertThrows`:

```java
@Test
void addNullSkuThrows() {
    IllegalArgumentException ex = assertThrows(
        IllegalArgumentException.class,
        () -> catalog.add(null, 1));
    assertTrue(ex.getMessage().contains("sku is required"));
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Catching `Exception` (too broad) can swallow unrelated errors and make the test pass incorrectly.

